Commands that evaluate their line again (/timer, /scon) evaluate what
someone said too, so it can run as code; $unsafe stops that, like mIRC's.

-- relay.mrc --
on *:TEXT:!later *:#:.timer 1 5 echo $chan later: $2-
on *:TEXT:!safe *:#:.timer 1 5 echo $chan safe: $unsafe($2-)
on *:TEXT:!all *:#:scon -a echo $chan all: $unsafe($2-)
-- transcript --
me trout
chan #trout @trout mallory
active #trout
< :mallory!m@host PRIVMSG #trout :!later I am $me
@ +5s
= #trout: later: I am trout
< :mallory!m@host PRIVMSG #trout :!safe I am $me %x $+ $chr(41)
@ +5s
= #trout: safe: I am $me %x $+ $chr(41)
< :mallory!m@host PRIVMSG #trout :!all $calc(1+1) [ $me ]
= #trout: all: $calc(1+1) [ $me ]
